      <div class="project-summary" data-scroll-group data-scroll-step="90">
        <p>As the site grew, I could remember a company, a place, or an idea without remembering which page held it. Search gave me and visitors a way to find those things again. I also wanted visitors to be able to ask a question and get a direct answer, even when the relevant material was spread across several pages. That became the purpose of <AiAskTerm />. Using it myself later opened up another possibility, exploring what familiar pieces might say together when read around a new question.</p>

        <p>I used the public material already on the site as the basis for that exploration. The text is indexed as passages that retain their original page and location. Projects, photographs, and interactive pieces also keep their own form, so the interface can return a passage or bring the original work into a new reading.</p>

        <p>Three experiences use that shared material. Search opens an original passage in context. <AiAskTerm /> brings passages together into an answer with citations. <AiViewTerm /> composes a reading path that includes the original work alongside an explanation of how it relates to the question. Each offers a different depth of exploration, from finding a particular item to reading across the archive.</p>
