      <section class="story-section" data-scroll-group data-scroll-step="90">
        <h2 id="grounded-ask"><AiAskTerm /> brings related passages into one answer</h2>
        <p>I wanted visitors to be able to ask a question about my work and get a useful answer straight away. A question such as how I use AI could draw on several projects, leaving someone to find and read each page before putting the answer together. I developed <AiAskTerm /> to bring that material into one direct response.</p>
        <p>To answer across several pages, a language model has to select what matters and explain how it relates to the question. I kept citations alongside that explanation so visitors could check its interpretation against the original work. The answer gives them a quick way to understand something, and the sources give them somewhere to continue if they want more detail.</p>
        <p>The browser prepares context from the public site and sends it with the question to a Cloudflare Worker, which requests the model’s answer. This is retrieval-augmented generation, or RAG. The current version supplies the main site material and the published fragments, using retrieval to bring relevant fragments forward. Keeping that broader context available helps with questions that connect several parts of the archive. The example below shows a cited answer, its sources, and suggested questions for continuing the exploration.</p>
        <SearchPalette
          embedded
          fixed-mode="ask"
          initial-query="How does Henry use AI in his personal website?"
          :initial-answer="savedAsk.answer"
