      <section class="story-section" data-scroll-group data-scroll-step="90">
        <h2 id="composed-views"><AiViewTerm /> reorganises the site around a question</h2>
        <p>Much of what I wanted to bring together already had a form worth reading or using. A project might have an interactive demo, photographs might belong in a gallery, and a fragment might express something in wording that mattered. An <AiAskTerm /> answer could describe and cite those pieces. Bringing them into the response itself would let someone explore a connection through the work, trying the demo or looking through the photographs as they read.</p>
        <p>This led to <AiViewTerm />, a response that takes the form of a composed page. A question, theme, or perspective guides the selection of material, and the narrative explains what the visitor should notice in it. A project’s original interaction can sit beside a research entry or a piece of personal writing, giving the explanation concrete material to work with.</p>
