        <p>To make that possible, I registered projects, research entries, fragments, image groups, and interactive components as reusable blocks. The model can select and arrange the relevant blocks, with their original source material intact, and write the text that connects them. Separating the source components from the new narrative lets the same work appear in different readings without having to recreate its demo or rewrite the fragment each time.</p>
        <p>A question about learning might bring together work on human cognition, an education project, and a fragment written in another context. A question about how I build tools might draw on some of those same pieces for different reasons. The composition changes which relationships come into view, while the original material remains available to explore.</p>
