        <p>I began saving <AiViewTerm plural /> that I wanted to return to. A question could produce an arrangement of the archive worth keeping, and asking it again later would happen against a collection that had grown. Preserving the reading meant keeping both the perspective and the material available when it was composed.</p>
        <p>There are two comparisons I find useful here. Different questions asked around the same time can reveal different relationships within the same archive. Returning to one question months later can show how new work or writing changes the context of older pieces. A saved <AiViewTerm /> gives each reading a place in that history.</p>
        <p>A saved <AiViewTerm /> keeps the question, composed page, illustrations, narration, sources, and creation date together as a snapshot. It receives a permanent link, and its creator can choose whether to include it in Shared Views. The examples below preserve the archive as it was read at those moments.</p>
