      <section class="story-section" data-scroll-group data-scroll-step="90">
        <h2 id="what-the-archive-gives-back" data-source-anchor="what-the-archive-gives-back">Returning to my own archive</h2>
        <p>Returning to these readings has changed what I can get from keeping an archive. A piece of writing records what I could articulate at the time. A later question can place it beside work or an experience that helps me understand it differently. The original piece remains, along with a record of how I came to read it later.</p>
        <p>Visitors extend that exploration with questions and perspectives I might never choose myself. Their <AiViewTerm plural /> can bring together parts of the site I usually think about separately. If they choose to share a reading, I and other visitors can return to the perspective they brought to the material.</p>
        <p>I want the site to support that continuing exchange between what I record and what I come to understand through it. Projects, experiences, photographs, and writing preserve parts of my life as they happen. The readings preserve ways of looking across that material, leaving room for new questions to change what I notice in it.</p>

